<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00VG">Remark <span data-tag="00VG">11.4.0.36</span>.</a> The definition of the pointed homotopy category $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}_{\ast }$ can be viewed as a special case of Construction <a data-tag="00LX" href="/tag/00LX">2.4.6.1</a>, applied to the simplicial category $(\operatorname{Set}_{\Delta }^{\circ })_{\ast }$ of Construction <a data-tag="00VF" href="/tag/00VF">11.4.0.35</a>. Invoking Proposition <a data-tag="00M4" href="/tag/00M4">2.4.6.9</a>, we see that the category $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}_{\ast }$ of Construction <a data-tag="00VE" href="/tag/00VE">3.2.1.12</a> can be identified with the homotopy category of the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{\ast }$ (as suggested by the notation). </p>
